[{:db/id 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" "question-35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" "question-2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" :question/id #uuid "42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-95349" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9da244a1-6637-5db7-b8ef-33283dce2b41"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9da244a1-6637-5db7-b8ef-33283dce2b41" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da244a1-6637-5db7-b8ef-33283dce2b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f6c601f-dc07-56ea-bef7-25b4a444358f" "answer-f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" "answer-226f1dbb-e586-5c42-93b7-43b8c5544971" "answer-6266bf60-cbee-534e-aaad-f1b70c7c6e56" "answer-e2b2ea65-38c0-59e1-8092-216f0cd8d2d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f6c601f-dc07-56ea-bef7-25b4a444358f" :answer/id #uuid "4f6c601f-dc07-56ea-bef7-25b4a444358f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15,\\,9,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer/id #uuid "f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-226f1dbb-e586-5c42-93b7-43b8c5544971" :answer/id #uuid "226f1dbb-e586-5c42-93b7-43b8c5544971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4,\\,3,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6266bf60-cbee-534e-aaad-f1b70c7c6e56" :answer/id #uuid "6266bf60-cbee-534e-aaad-f1b70c7c6e56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5,\\,4,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2b2ea65-38c0-59e1-8092-216f0cd8d2d3" :answer/id #uuid "e2b2ea65-38c0-59e1-8092-216f0cd8d2d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" :question/id #uuid "35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95362" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =8,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ee60de8-7912-55ad-80bc-fd51fae2e264"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ee60de8-7912-55ad-80bc-fd51fae2e264" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee60de8-7912-55ad-80bc-fd51fae2e264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer-field/choices ["answer-903124f2-18ad-506a-90f1-7a04c1d43894" "answer-03cdbbac-81f1-5a5a-8c0b-cc9eada2874c" "answer-62cb00c2-7471-5b2f-86f0-ee1821df8b74" "answer-a9a954e9-faca-5755-872b-2adf607495f9" "answer-e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-903124f2-18ad-506a-90f1-7a04c1d43894" :answer/id #uuid "903124f2-18ad-506a-90f1-7a04c1d43894" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03cdbbac-81f1-5a5a-8c0b-cc9eada2874c" :answer/id #uuid "03cdbbac-81f1-5a5a-8c0b-cc9eada2874c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62cb00c2-7471-5b2f-86f0-ee1821df8b74" :answer/id #uuid "62cb00c2-7471-5b2f-86f0-ee1821df8b74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9a954e9-faca-5755-872b-2adf607495f9" :answer/id #uuid "a9a954e9-faca-5755-872b-2adf607495f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer/id #uuid "e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{8}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" :question/id #uuid "2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95374" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974" :answer-field/id #uuid "2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" "answer-8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" "answer-22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" "answer-7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" "answer-c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/id #uuid "8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/id #uuid "22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/id #uuid "7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/id #uuid "c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8,\\,4,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" "question-9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" :question/id #uuid "9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" :question/math-academy-id "q-95375" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )[(5-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4)]-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +16)-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b838eb18-ab2d-5fe6-b6c3-92ea8e153a8c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b838eb18-ab2d-5fe6-b6c3-92ea8e153a8c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b838eb18-ab2d-5fe6-b6c3-92ea8e153a8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5febb191-7c5d-5f4e-82d6-efc23b4d4485" "answer-9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" "answer-be6dbb3a-d9f4-5182-87d2-f89ac41af4ff" "answer-73c9cf54-1f9b-52f1-b8ed-dd9e193c12b3" "answer-2f16480c-d86a-5db9-b802-4ced71c8377c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5febb191-7c5d-5f4e-82d6-efc23b4d4485" :answer/id #uuid "5febb191-7c5d-5f4e-82d6-efc23b4d4485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16,\\,9,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" :answer/id #uuid "9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be6dbb3a-d9f4-5182-87d2-f89ac41af4ff" :answer/id #uuid "be6dbb3a-d9f4-5182-87d2-f89ac41af4ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5,\\,3,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73c9cf54-1f9b-52f1-b8ed-dd9e193c12b3" :answer/id #uuid "73c9cf54-1f9b-52f1-b8ed-dd9e193c12b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f16480c-d86a-5db9-b802-4ced71c8377c" :answer/id #uuid "2f16480c-d86a-5db9-b802-4ced71c8377c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},\\,2,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" :question/id #uuid "9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-95378" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954" :answer-field/id #uuid "646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6eb0c7d-ecb7-57ee-81fb-a558588e214e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e594ce1-22ea-5fd6-afb9-6b06b4b9255c" "answer-70323d57-c32e-523a-902e-eb0de24ca0c0" "answer-83f12e6b-62c0-5595-a194-e0065cfb501d" "answer-c6eb0